Subject: [Vita] Bound Ruby worker startup without exposing reclaimed thread state

Use a five-second realtime deadline and an atomic ready/cancel decision. Fresh
and cached children prepare stack/TLS through a separate two-owner record;
only accepted children may dereference the Ruby thread. Reuse the interrupt
pair, and cap unreclaimable no-entry records at eight instead of allocating
unbounded tombstones. A late child releases its record without running Ruby.
Timed waits use realtime on this build; a forward clock step larger than the deadline can end the wait early.
Cancellation remains safe: a late child sees 'cancelled', and the only effect is a spurious ThreadError.

